= The Market for Proxy Advice

== Origins

#slide[
  === Two firms advise holders of most of the shares voted at U.S. annual meetings.

  - ISS and Glass Lewis together hold over 90% of the market for proxy advice.
]

#slide[
  === What made proxy advisors powerful.

  - The 2003 rule made every fund adviser vote its proxies in its clients' interest and disclose how.

  - Buying a recommendation was the cheapest way to show that a vote was considered.
]
